course: dictionary
lesson: 7786
title: One word, many meanings: Qing
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Qing is not an English word, so you cannot find its meaning from sounds you already know. But you can use context. Look at the words around it, and check if they name a place, a time, or a sound. «The Qing dynasty, 1644–1912, was founded by the Manchus from the northeast.» Here Qing is a name for a royal family that ruled China.
explain: In Mandarin, the same sound can change meaning with its tone, the way the pitch goes up or down. Read «qǐng» (please), «qīng» (clear or light) and «qíng» (feeling, or sunny weather) as three different words. The sentence around the word tells you which one it is. In pinyin, «q» sounds like English «ch», so «qing» sounds like «ching».
explain: A good check is to swap in your meaning and see if it still makes sense. If you read «qǐng zuò» in a classroom, it means please sit down, because a teacher is being polite. Then in history, «the Qing dynasty» is always a name, never a polite request.
fact: Qing was the last dynasty of emperors to rule China, from 1644 to 1912.
fact: The Qing were founded by the Manchu people, from the northeast.
fact: In pinyin, «qǐng» means please, «qīng» means clear or light, and «qíng» means feeling or sunny weather.
fact: «Qingming» is a festival when families sweep their ancestors' graves.
exercise: «The Qing dynasty ruled China until 1912.» What does Qing mean in this sentence? | *The name of China's last royal family of emperors | A clear, light tea | A new kind of bicycle | A Chinese festival for sweeping graves
exercise: In Mandarin, «qǐng zuò» means what? | *Please sit down | Clear and light | Feeling or sunny weather | Goodbye
exercise: In pinyin, the letter «q» sounds most like which English sound? | *ch | sh | k | th
test: Mandarin «qīng» means? | Ancient | Feeling or sunny weather | Please | *Clear or light
test: Which festival is it when families sweep their ancestors' graves? | *Qingming | Mid-Autumn | Diwali | Lunar New Year
exam: The Qing dynasty was founded by which people? | *Manchus | Mongols | Japanese | Tibetans
